Pooled solvers now have a separate, configurable idle-handshake safety timeout
(/solverIdleTimeout, default 300 seconds), replacing the 100 ms scheduling
deadline. Stdout EOF and transport failures retire dead solvers promptly. The
hidden /legacySolverIdleTimeout:1 restores the original 100 ms policy for
comparison and migration. This changes solver reuse, not verification conditions;
retaining a solver's native history can affect subsequent resource counts.
